I step out of the building.
I go to the nearby kirana store.
There is a small crowd in the shop.
I wait for my turn.
The shopkeeper looks at me.
I say to him, "Dada, first give me half a kilo of thick poha."
He fills the poha in a bag and weighs it.
Then I tell him the next item.
"Give me a small packet of raw peanuts."
He puts the packet of peanuts with the poha.
He asks me, "Madam, do you want anything else?"
I look at my list.
I say, "No, that's it."
"How much is the bill?"
He says, "Seventy-five rupees."
I give him the money.
After that, I pick up my bag.
Now I am done buying the dry groceries.
Now I just need to buy fresh vegetables.
